  "live_records": {
    "q-90563": {
      "dom_id": "step-q90563",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{8},\\, & 0\\le x\\le 4, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the variance using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we compute $\\text{E}[X]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}x\\cdot \\frac{x}{8}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{3}}{24}|}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{x}{8}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{{x}^{3}}{8}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{4}}{32}|}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =8-{(\\frac{8}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
