    "q-90562": {
      "dom_id": "step-q90562",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{2x}{15},\\, & 1\\le x\\le 4, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the variance using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we compute $\\text{E}[X]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}x\\cdot (\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{2x}{15})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}(\\frac{2x}{3}-\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{15})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{45})|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}{x}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{2x}{15})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}(\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{15})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{9}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{30})|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{2}-{(\\frac{11}{5})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{33}{50} \\\\  & =0.66.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
