    "q-90604": {
      "dom_id": "step-q90604",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "The continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$ stated below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]=0.65,$ compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{5}, & 0<x<1, \\\\ \\frac{1}{{x}^{6}}, & 1\\le x, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the variance using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}],$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{4}{5}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{x}^{6}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{4{x}^{2}}{5}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{4{x}^{3}}{15}|}_{0}^{1}+{(-\\frac{1}{3{x}^{3}})|}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =0.6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =0.6-(0.65)^{2} \\\\  & ≈0.18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nrounded to $2$ decimal places.",
